ubaru's number for this recall is WUM-98.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":366282,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=19V701000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":4,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2015","make":"SUBARU","model":"FORESTER"},{"year":"2017","make":"SUBARU","model":"FORESTER"},{"year":"2016","make":"SUBARU","model":"FORESTER"},{"year":"2018","make":"SUBARU","model":"FORESTER"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false},{"campaign":"18V455000","received":"2018-07-10","manufacturer":"Subaru of America, Inc.","component":"TIRES","summary":"Subaru of America, Inc. (Subaru) is recalling certain 2018 Subaru Forester vehicles.  The Certification Label may indicate the incorrect wheel size, tire size, and air pressure.  As such, these vehicles fail to comply with the requirements of Federal Motor Vehicle Safety Standard (FMVSS) number 110, \"Tire Selection and Rims.\"","consequence":"Installing incorrect tires or applying incorrect tire air pressure may increase the risk of a crash.","remedy":"Subaru will notify owners, and dealers will install a corrected label, free of charge.  The recall began July 26, 2018.  Owners may contact Subaru customer service at 1-844-373-6614.  Subaru's number for this recall is WTS-78.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":3654,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=18V455000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":1,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2018","make":"SUBARU","model":"FORESTER"}],"campaign_vehicles_truncated":false}]}
